  form she has a circular crown  and a halo but one of makikula's curses  attaches itself to noel's shoulder and  back  and just kind of drains her power away i  am assuming that this curse is just an  effect of decaying world  not an actual long lasting curse like  the one that affected her mother and  loro but we'll have to wait and see  mkikula even tries to explain using cold  hard logic that no matter what noel does  now  winning this fight is impossible what is  even the point of resisting  this irrational aspect of human nature  is both fascinating  and confusing for megicula at the same  time though  megikula realizes that this is probably  why humans are occasionally capable of  generating magic beyond her expectations  humans are not always rational creatures  sometimes they kick logic to the curb  and make the impossible possible to  quote my boy kamina from gurren lagann  and this is what makes humans so  unpredictable  nevertheless megikula is confident that  no human will ever be able to defeat her  within the confines of her decaying  world  spell devils seem to be more rational  than humans because they would never  fight someone that they have no  realistic chance of defeating at least i  assume that's the devils that magikala  knows personally because we all know  that our boy liba  is just crazy enough to do it from  megicula's perspective  humans are weird creatures and they are  willing to sacrifice their very lives  for meaningless things  like ossie sacrificing her life for her  children and gaia sacrificing his life  for loro pachika  i mean those things are meaningless for  someone like megikula but they are  certainly not meaningless for the people  doing the sacrificing and just like her  mother before her  even now against all odds noel is still  refusing to give up  because of some vague and illogical idea  of hope  throughout this whole conversation with  megikula noel is fully aware that she  has no chance of winning  but that is what 